              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "AIS asks for the financial year. Form 26AS on TRACES asks for the assessment year. For income earned from April 2025 to March 2026, select FY 2025-26 in AIS but AY 2026-27 in Form 26AS. Mixing them up is the fastest way to confuse yourself.",
              "_key": "k29"
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "Downloading and opening the files",
              "headers": [
                "Item",
                "Detail"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k31",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "AIS formats",
                    "PDF, JSON or CSV. CSV is easiest for sorting and totalling in a spreadsheet."
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k33",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "TIS format",
                    "PDF"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k35",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "PDF password",
                    "Your PAN in lower case followed by your date of birth as DDMMYYYY, with no space"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k37",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Password example",
                    "PAN ABCDE1234F, born 15 April 1990: abcde1234f15041990"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k39",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "On your phone",
                    "The AIS for Taxpayer app shows the same information"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k40"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k41",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k42",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Inside AIS: Two Parts, Seven Sections",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k43",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k44",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Part A",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k45",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " holds your identity details: PAN, name, date of birth, and contact details. ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k46",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Part B",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k47",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " holds everything reported against your PAN, grouped into sections.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "AIS Part B sections",
              "headers": [
                "Section",
                "What it contains"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k49",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "TDS and TCS information",
                    "Every TDS and TCS entry, including salary, interest, dividends and TCS on remittances"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k51",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "SFT information",
                    "Reports from banks, registrars, depositories and others: interest, dividends, securities and mutual fund transactions, high-value deposits and purchases"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k53",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Payment of taxes",
                    "Advance tax and self-assessment tax paid by challan"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k55",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Demand and refund",
                    "Tax demands raised and refunds initiated during the year"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k57",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Pending proceedings",
                    "Proceedings under the Income-tax Act still open against your PAN"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k59",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Completed proceedings",
                    "Proceedings that have been concluded"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k61",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Other information",
                    "Other data received by the department, such as salary details from employers' statements, interest on refunds and foreign remittances"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k62"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k63",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k64",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Reading the Information Codes",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k65",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k66",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Every AIS entry carries an information code showing where it came from. TDS entries are labelled with the TDS section, and SFT entries carry SFT codes. These are the ones a salaried investor sees most often:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "What it reports",
                "Typical source"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k68",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "TDS-192",
                    "Salary and TDS on it",
                    "Your employer"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k70",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "TDS-194A",
                    "Interest, such as on FDs, with TDS",
                    "Bank or NBFC"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k72",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "TDS-194",
                    "Dividends with TDS",
                    "Listed company"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k74",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "SFT-015",
                    "Dividend income",
                    "Company or its registrar"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k76",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "SFT-016",
                    "Interest income",
                    "Bank, post office"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k78",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "SFT-017",
                    "Sale and purchase of securities",
                    "Depository or stock exchange"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k80",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "SFT-018",
                    "Sale and purchase of mutual fund units",
                    "Mutual fund registrar such as CAMS or KFintech"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k81"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k82",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k83",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "TIS: The Summary Built From AIS",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k84",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k85",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "AIS lists every report separately. If SBI credits interest quarterly, or a fund house reports each redemption, you see many lines. TIS rolls them up into categories such as salary, interest from deposits, dividend and sale of mutual fund units, and shows three values for each category.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "The three value columns in TIS",
              "headers": [
                "Column",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k87",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Reported value",
                    "The total as reported by all information sources, before any clean-up"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k89",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Processed value",
                    "The value after the system removes duplicates using pre-defined rules"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k91",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Derived value",
                    "The value after considering your feedback on AIS entries, along with the processed value"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k92"
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "AIS is the evidence. TIS is the summary. The derived value in TIS is what pre-fills your return, so check every TIS figure against the AIS entries behind it.",
              "_key": "k93"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k94",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k95",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "How Duplicates Are Removed",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k96",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k97",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The same income often reaches the department twice: once through a TDS statement and once through SFT. Rakesh, an engineer in Coimbatore, received a dividend of ₹14,000 from Infosys in FY 2025-26. Because it crossed ₹10,000, TDS of 10% (₹1,400) was deducted under section 194. The registrar also reported the same dividend under SFT-015. So his AIS shows two entries for one dividend.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k98",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k99",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "For dividends, the rule is that for each reporting entity, the higher of the amount reported under SFT-015 and the amount reported by the deductor under section 194 is kept, and the other is marked as a duplicate.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "Rakesh's dividend category in TIS",
              "headers": [
                "Column",
                "Amount (₹)",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k101",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Reported value",
                    "28,000",
                    "₹14,000 from TDS-194 plus ₹14,000 from SFT-015"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k103",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Processed value",
                    "14,000",
                    "One entry kept, the other marked duplicate"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k105",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Derived value",
                    "14,000",
                    "No feedback given, so it equals the processed value"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k106"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k107",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k108",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Priya's TIS",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k109",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k110",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Here is how Priya's FY 2025-26 information rolls up in TIS, based on what was reported to the department.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "Priya's TIS, FY 2025-26 (derived values)",
              "headers": [
                "Category",
                "Derived value (₹)",
                "Built from"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k112",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Salary",
                    "18,00,000",
                    "Employer's salary TDS statements"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k114",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Interest from deposit",
                    "1,00,000",
                    "SBI ₹38,000 and ICICI Bank ₹62,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k116",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Dividend",
                    "6,000",
                    "HDFC Bank, reported under SFT-015"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k118",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Sale of mutual fund units",
                    "2,40,000",
                    "Registrar report under SFT-018"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k119"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "TIS is not your taxable income. The ₹2,40,000 against sale of mutual fund units is the sale value, not the capital gain. Priya's gain depends on what she paid for those units, which she must work out from her capital gains statement from CAMS, KFintech or Zerodha. Similarly, salary in TIS is gross salary before exemptions and deductions.",
              "_key": "k120"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k121",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k122",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "AIS, TIS and Form 26AS Side by Side",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "comparison",
              "title": "AIS vs TIS",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "_key": "k124",
                  "label": "AIS",
                  "points": [
                    "Every individual report against your PAN",
                    "Shows the source and information code of each entry",
                    "Where you give feedback on wrong entries",
                    "Downloads as PDF, JSON or CSV",
                    "Use it to investigate and prove"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k126",
                  "label": "TIS",
                  "points": [
                    "Totals by category, such as interest or dividend",
                    "Shows reported, processed and derived values",
                    "Updates automatically when you give feedback in AIS",
                    "Derived values pre-fill your return",
                    "Use it to check what the return will assume"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k127"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "From tax year 2026-27, the information in AIS and Form 26AS is brought together as Form 168 under the Income-tax Act, 2025. TIS and the feedback facility continue, so everything in this chapter still applies.",
              "_key": "k128"
            },
            {
              "_type": "toolLink",
              "label": "AIS help page, Income Tax Department",
              "url": "https://www.incometax.gov.in/iec/foportal/help/all-topics/e-filing-services/ais-annual-information-statement",
              "description": "Official guide to viewing AIS and TIS, downloading them and giving feedback.",
              "_key": "k129"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k130",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k131",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Check Your Understanding",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "quiz",
              "title": "Open the PDF",
              "question": "Ananya's PAN is PQRST6789K and she was born on 3 November 1995. What is the password for her AIS PDF?",
              "options": [
                "PQRST6789K03111995",
                "pqrst6789k03111995",
                "03111995",
                "pqrst6789k"
              ],
              "correctIndex": 1,
              "explanation": "The AIS PDF password is the PAN in lower case followed by the date of birth as DDMMYYYY, with no space: pqrst6789k03111995.",
              "_key": "k132"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "numericInput",
              "title": "Remove the duplicate",
              "prompt": "Deepa received a dividend of ₹22,000 from ITC in FY 2025-26. Her AIS shows it twice: once under TDS-194 and once under SFT-015, both for ₹22,000. With no feedback given, what should the processed value for dividend in her TIS be?",
              "correctValue": 22000,
              "tolerance": 0,
              "unit": "₹",
              "explanation": "For dividends from the same reporting entity, the higher of the SFT-015 and TDS-194 amounts is kept and the other is marked as a duplicate. Both are ₹22,000, so the processed value is ₹22,000, not ₹44,000.",
              "_key": "k133"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "fillInTheBlank",
              "title": "Which value pre-fills?",
              "textWithBlank": "The ___ value in TIS, which reflects your feedback, is used to pre-fill your income tax return.",
              "correctAnswers": [
                "derived"
              ],
              "explanation": "TIS shows reported, processed and derived values. The derived value takes your feedback into account and is used for pre-filling.",
              "_key": "k134"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "scenario",
              "title": "Tanvi's scary number",
              "scenario": "Tanvi, a marketing executive in Ahmedabad, opens her TIS for FY 2025-26 and sees \"Sale of securities and units of mutual fund: ₹8,50,000\". Her salary is already fully taxed through TDS. She panics that she will now owe tax on another ₹8.5 lakh of income.",
              "prompt": "Is she right to panic? What should she do?",
              "modelAnswer": "No. ₹8,50,000 is the total sale value of shares and fund units she sold, not her income. What is taxable is the capital gain: sale value minus cost, split into short term and long term. She should open the AIS entries behind that figure under SFT-017 and SFT-018 to see each sale, then download her capital gains statement from her broker, such as Zerodha's tax P&L, and from CAMS or KFintech for mutual funds. She reports the gains, not the sale value, in the capital gains schedule of her return. If her sales were at a loss, she may even have losses to report.",
              "_key": "k135"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "checklist",
              "title": "Your first AIS review",
              "steps": [
                "Open AIS for FY 2025-26 and confirm Part A shows your correct name, PAN and date of birth.",
                "Download AIS as CSV and TIS as PDF.",
                "List every category in TIS with its derived value.",
                "For each TIS category, open the AIS entries behind it and check the sources are yours.",
                "Note any entry that is wrong, duplicated or not yours, for feedback.",
                "Mark sale values from SFT-017 and SFT-018 as needing a capital gains calculation, not direct income."
              ],
              "_key": "k136"
            },
            {
              "_type": "keyTakeaways",
              "points": [
                "Open AIS from Services on the e-filing portal, and select the financial year, not the assessment year.",
                "The AIS PDF password is your PAN in lower case followed by your date of birth as DDMMYYYY.",
                "AIS lists every report against your PAN, grouped into seven Part B sections, each entry with an information code.",
                "TIS rolls AIS up by category with reported, processed and derived values.",
                "Processed values remove duplicates, such as a dividend reported under both TDS-194 and SFT-015.",
                "The derived value pre-fills your return, but TIS figures such as sale value are not taxable income by themselves."
              ],
              "_key": "k137"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "disclaimer",
              "text": "This lesson is for education only and reflects the AIS and TIS layout as of September 2026. PANs, dates and amounts are illustrative, and portal menus can change. For your specific situation, check the e-filing portal or consult a chartered accountant.",
